# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Compiled binaries. Go executables on Linux/macOS have no extension, so the
# *.exe rule above won't catch them. Build into bin/ (e.g. `go build -o bin/server ./cmd/server`).
/bin/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts. Anchored to the repo root:
# an unanchored coverage.* once hid vendor/golang.org/x/text/language/coverage.go,
# so fresh clones could not build.
/*.out
/coverage.*
/*.coverprofile
/profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

*.log

# Python bytecode (tools/, db/seed/)
__pycache__/
